   - Circuit Breaker:
            (In General, if a Circuit is Closed means Connected; and Circuit is Open means DisConnected.)
            - Resilience 4j is used for Circuit Breaker.
            - Circuit Breaker has 3 states. Server can be in-
                CLOSED -> when one service can able to call another service without any errors / when one service calling other service and the other service is Up and able to respond and services can able to send requests and respond to each other.
                OPEN -> If 50% requests fail. then Circuit will be Open. Then, Requests will not go through. (and we can show some fallback error at this time...)
                            and we can configure, when again to Close the Circuit. lets say, if need to Closed after 10mins, then first it comes HALF_OPEN state.
                HALF_OPEN -> Now here, calls will happen. if requests are successful then Circuit will be CLOSED.
                                If Calls are failed here, again it goes to OPEN state.
        - First we need add Resilience4j dependency in the project.
        - and in the application.properties file,
                resilience4j.circuitbreaker.instances.(// here some circuit breaker name which can be anything)nameCB.register-health-indicator=true
                resilience4j.circuitbreaker.instances.nameCB.sliding-window-size=5 (// means takes 5 requests)
                resilience4j.circuitbreaker.instances.nameCB.failure-rate-threshold=50 (//if 50% fails, circuit needs to be OPEN)
                resilience4j.circuitbreaker.instances.nameCB.wait-duration-in-open-state=10 (//how much time needs to wait in OPEN state - 10secs and goes to HALF_OPEN state)
                resilience4j.circuitbreaker.instances.nameCB.permitted-number-of-calls-in-half-open-state=2 (// how many calls needs to be made and need to verify whether circuit needs to be OPEN or HALF_OPEN )
                resilience4j.circuitbreaker.instances.nameCB.automatic-transition-from-open-to-half-open-enabled=true
                resilience4j.circuitbreaker.instances.nameCB.minimum-number-of-calls=3

        - and also to which endpoints Circuit Breaker needs to be used, we need to annotate that method with @CircuitBreaker(name = "nameCB", fallbackMethod = "userNotResponding")  "userNotResponding" - this is method name not message. we need to write that fallback method.

   - Kafka:
            There are two ways of communication - Synchronous and Asynchronous.
            we know that, Inter service communication: Rest Template, Feign Client. These are Synchronous Communication.
            Synchronous Communication: When Service A sends a request to Service B, Until Service B sending response to Service A, Service A will be blocked.
            Asynchronous Communication: here it will not wait for the response from the server.
            - Kafka is used in Asynchronous mode for Communication. (RabbitMQ is also for Asynchronous Communication)
                    - It needs to be installed in system. It runs on its own port. It works independently in our system.
                    - Every Kafka Server is called as 'Broker'.
                        Every 'Broker' has 'Topics'. Every 'Topics' a 'Partition'. Every 'Partition' has a 'Offset'. Every Kafka 'Broker' has some 'Producers' , 'Consumers'. Kafka has 'Zookeeper'.
                        Broker : It is a kind of Server. where kafka related all things happen here. kafka can have multiple Brokers. means multiple instances. default port is 9092.
                        Topic : Topic is like a shelf, which contains multiple messages in it.
                (In Kafka, when a message is Published(in kafka published means Sent) from Service A, if it want to send to Service B, it first Published/sent to Kafka Broker's Topic i.e a Topic in Kafka Broker - This is called 'Fire and Forget')
                        Producer : which service sends a message are Producers.
                        Consumer : which service reads it are Consumers.
                                    (
                                        Library = Broker
                                        Shelf = Topic
                                        Shelf has Partitions which ordered as queue. Consumers can read parallelly.
                                            means, if in a shelf, if there are 3 partitions, all three partition's first message is read at a time..
                                        Books = messages
                                    )
                        Offsets : It is a number given to a message. a token number. it is a continuous sequence. it starts from 0. Kafka registers/notes these numbers.
                                        Every partition has its own Offset.
                                  it looks something like,
                                        Partition 1 -> offset 0,1 (// here 1 will be the last read message)
                                        Partition 2 -> offset 0
                                        Partition 3 -> offset 1,2,3
                                        Partition 1 -> offset 2 (// as the last offset was 1, now it starts(consumes) from 2)
                                            Parallel Processing.
                        Consumer Group : multiple Consumers reading one Topic.
                    - There will be huge META DATA, like how many brokers, how many producers, how many consumers, how many messages, etc..
                            This META DATA is maintained by 'ZooKeeper'. Zookeeper server maintain the META DATA of Kafka.
                            Kafka 3 has Zookeeper, but in kafka 4, Zookeeper is removed.
                    - Inplace of Zookeeper, 'KRaft' concept was introduced. (KRaft - Kafka Raft Metadata Mode) It is an alternative for Zookeeper.
                        (Raft means, choosing a leader. Raft = consensus algorithm)
                        (There will be a Retention period of 7 days)

            - we can handle Kafka in Terminal with commands.
                    and we can also handle by creating a separate project and adding Kafka dependency in it. There will be two projects one for Producer and another for Consumer.